{#
  Rumor mill — what travelers, merchants, and NPCs are gossiping about.
  Drawn from real events across all players' sessions.

  Use in tavern scenes, market conversations, NPC small talk.
  The rumors are TRUE (they happened to other players) but arrive
  distorted through the grapevine.
#}

{% set rumors = getRumors() %}
{% if rumors and rumors.length > 0 %}
<rumorMill>
Recent rumors circulating among travelers and merchants (these are based on real events elsewhere in the world — use 1-2 naturally in NPC dialogue when appropriate, especially in social settings like taverns, markets, or campfires):
{% for rumor in rumors %}
  <rumor>{{ rumor }}</rumor>
{% endfor %}
Present rumors as hearsay: "I heard that...", "They say...", "A merchant told me...". Distort slightly — the grapevine never gets it exactly right. NPCs may disagree about details.
</rumorMill>
{% endif %}
